Technical
### Changed

- Update the Anthropic, coverlet.collector, and Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI NuGet dependencies. ([#328](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/328))

### Added

- **Breaking:** Remove pull request descriptions from `changelog.json` and store complete fact entries, including descriptions, in the run record. Read fact bases from run records instead of `changelog.json`. ([#294](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/294))
- **Breaking:** Make `preview` show the facts and planned model calls without making model calls or writing files. ([#292](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/292))
- Show run outcomes in the summary’s opening line, identify each audience’s rendering, and group the command help by purpose. ([#342](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/342))
- Group `doctor` checks by area, show statuses with symbols and words, and explain whether warnings affect a run. ([#341](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/341))
- Show run progress with a terminal-aware spinner and add the `--plain` option to every command. ([#340](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/340))
- Quote pull request titles and descriptions in prompts, neutralize embedded title and description tags, and truncate long descriptions in prompts. ([#338](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/338))
- Refuse to replace a published release unless `generate` is given `--replace-published`. ([#335](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/335))
- Show the version-specific configuration template when `doctor` cannot find `chartula.yaml`. ([#329](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/329))
- Show each run step’s progress, including commit counts and elapsed time, on stderr. ([#297](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/297))
- Add `chartula doctor` to check whether the setup needed for a run is ready. ([#295](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/295))
- Derive closed issue numbers from the text the model reads at every fact-base depth, and map legacy depth values to `title-and-description`. ([#293](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/293))
- Include direct commits alongside pull requests, while skipping merge commits without pull requests. ([#291](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/291))
- Add `chartula --version` to print the installed informational version. ([#286](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/286))
- Allow first-tag ranges and confirm first-tag or large ranges before reading them; use `--yes` to confirm without a prompt. ([#282](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/282))

### Fixed

- Correct the help grouping so each option appears once, and update the roadmap and CLI documentation. ([#344](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/344))
- Normalize whitespace and remove code fences when comparing names in the rule-based faithfulness check. ([#336](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/336))
- Write a fixed explanatory sentence to `CHANGELOG.md` and release notes when no changes reach technical readers, while keeping `renderings.technical` empty. ([#333](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/333))
- Use relaxed JSON escaping for `changelog.json` and the run record so characters are more readable while preserving their parsed values. ([#332](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/332))
- Separate review flags from the final entry of a rendering with a blank line and a `Flagged for review:` heading. ([#331](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/331))
- Identify unset or blank credential variables as unauthenticated in the run header. ([#330](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/330))
- Validate command-line options before a command starts, reject unknown or misplaced options, and honor `-h` and `--help` after a command. ([#301](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/301))
- Append a trailing slash to a GitHub API base URL when it is provided without one. ([#290](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/290))
- Treat an empty `filter.excludeCategories` list as a value that excludes no categories. ([#289](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/289))
- Report a model response the SDK cannot parse as unreadable rather than unreachable. ([#288](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/288))
- Refuse to run when both `chartula.yaml` and `chartula.yml` are present. ([#287](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/287))
- Check that the token can publish before the first model call in `generate`. ([#285](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/285))
- Clarify that `--no-publish` writes every file and omits only GitHub release notes. ([#284](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/284))

